<title>USA: Steck-Vaughn says Kopec resigns as CEO.</title>
<headline>Steck-Vaughn says Kopec resigns as CEO.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Steck-Vaughn Publishing Corp said Wednesday Anita Kopec, its president and chief executive officer, resigned to pursue other interests.</p>
<p>The publisher said James Levy, president of the Education and Trade Group of Harcourt General Inc subsidiary Harcourt Brace &amp; Co will take over Kopec's duties until a successor is named. It added Harcourt owns about 82 percent of Steck-Vaughn's outstanding stock.</p>
<p>Vice president and sales manager Mark Moyer also resigned.</p>
</text>
